A||N||2||chris6878||V6 rpm?||||5||
Z||000000||chris6878||12-19-1999||05:09 PM||||what is the normal idle for the v6...   when my idle drops under 1000 rpm's... my oil pressure light flickers sometimes...   i thought the engine may be running to slow to keep up the pressure.    i am presently trying to figure out a vaccum prob... when rpm is 1000 or greater, the oil pressure is fine....    (this is a newly rebuild engine)<P>Thanks<BR>chris||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||12-19-1999||05:50 PM||||I rebuilt an engine that had low oil pressure when it warmed up at an idle. I thought it was excessive clearance in the bearings due to a failure of some sort. When I pulled the oil pan down to check it out I discovered that the bearings were fine and that I didn't tighten the oil pump bolts. I tightened them, put the thing back together and the oil pressure was right were it should be. I had a good mechanical gauge hooked up to it to confirm that the oil pressure was really low.<p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 12-19-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||12-19-1999||07:41 PM||||Target idle in the computer is 900 RPM.<P>Oil pressure spec is 10 PSI minimum at 500 RPM and 50-55 PSI at 2000 RPM.<P>The easiest way to check the 500 RPM spec, is to disconnect the 4 way connector on the distributor to kill the ignition and injector pulses and crank the engine which is around 400 RPM or so. The pressure should be around 10 PSI or greater. Give it a second or two to build up.<P>Depending on the miles on your motor, the mains and cam bearings could be wearing. Also, the oil pump gear to cover clearance could be increasing from wear.<P>Answer, if it meets these specs, leave it alone.<P>Finally, the light flicker on RPM dip could be just a reflection of the wearing of the engine. If the light is off at normal 900 RPM idle and the oil pressure is above 10-15 PSI, then again, normal. Also, the fuel pressure switch kills the fuel at 4 PSI if that tells you anything.<P>All pressures at normal operating coolant temp.<P>TK<P>||||reg||1
